    {
      "x": 80,
      "y": 250,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:cue-step-1",
      "type": "geo",
      "props": {
        "w": 560,
        "h": 200,
        "geo": "rectangle",
        "dash": "draw",
        "growY": 12,
        "url": "",
        "scale": 1,
        "flipX": false,
        "flipY": false,
        "color": "orange",
        "labelColor": "black",
        "fill": "semi",
        "size": "m",
        "font": "sans",
        "align": "start",
        "verticalAlign": "middle",
        "richText": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "1 · Read the top pair first. This is a conformance diff drawn by SystemSketch itself, not a second picture of it. On estimate(), the struck row 'callee' is a port the target asserts and this board does not have; the red dashed cable is the connection that would have run through it."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "parentId": "page:page",
      "index": "aCwev",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    {
      "x": 760,
      "y": 1320,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:cue-pass",
      "type": "geo",
      "props": {
        "w": 1300,
        "h": 150,
        "geo": "rectangle",
        "dash": "draw",
        "growY": 0,
        "url": "",
        "scale": 1,
        "flipX": false,
        "flipY": false,
        "color": "green",
        "labelColor": "black",
        "fill": "semi",
        "size": "m",
        "font": "sans",
        "align": "start",
        "verticalAlign": "middle",
        "richText": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "PASS WHEN · The top pair reads as one graph whose two Blocks are visibly marked and whose missing port sits in its own struck row; the bottom pair looks completely untouched; and after Clear diff marks the whole board looks like the bottom pair, with the ghost rows and the red dashed cable gone."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "parentId": "page:page",
      "index": "aH7SE",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    {
      "x": 1300,
      "y": 60,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:cue-step-2",
      "type": "geo",
      "props": {
        "w": 620,
        "h": 140,
        "geo": "rectangle",
        "dash": "draw",
        "growY": 12,
        "url": "",
        "scale": 1,
        "flipX": false,
        "flipY": false,
        "color": "orange",
        "labelColor": "black",
        "fill": "semi",
        "size": "m",
        "font": "sans",
        "align": "start",
        "verticalAlign": "middle",
        "richText": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "2 · On transform(), the row reading 'callee → callable' is one renamed port, not a removal beside an addition. Below it sits the second ghost row the missing cable lands on."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "parentId": "page:page",
      "index": "aDyPn",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    {
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "z": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "camera:page:page",
      "typeName": "camera"
    },
    {
      "x": 80,
      "y": 700,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:cue-step-3",
      "type": "geo",
      "props": {
        "w": 560,
        "h": 150,
        "geo": "rectangle",
        "dash": "draw",
        "growY": 2,
        "url": "",
        "scale": 1,
        "flipX": false,
        "flipY": false,
        "color": "orange",
        "labelColor": "black",
        "fill": "semi",
        "size": "m",
        "font": "sans",
        "align": "start",
        "verticalAlign": "middle",
        "richText": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "3 · Now the bottom pair. It carries no marks at all, because nothing about it is wrong. A passing conformance case has to look exactly like this — an ordinary board."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "parentId": "page:page",
      "index": "aEnza",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    {
      "x": 0,
